      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Now flip it, because the math cuts both ways. One percent worse every day, repeated for a year, does not just stall you. It drags you down toward nearly nothing. This is the hidden danger of small choices. A skipped workout, one more late night, a tiny shortcut, each so minor you barely notice. But compounded in the wrong direction, they quietly hollow you out while you tell yourself it is fine.",
